detaileddescription.para:
The block-tridiagional matrix is updated by adding the term $ \Xi \mathcal{S} \Xi^\top $, where                    \[\begin{aligned}
\Xi &= \begin{pmatrix}
B_0^{\phantom\top} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \cdots & F_{N-1}^{\phantom\top} \\
F_0^{\phantom\top} & B_1^{\phantom\top} & 0 & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
0 & F_1^{\phantom\top} & B_2^{\phantom\top} & 0 & \cdots & 0 \\
0 & 0 & F_2^{\phantom\top} & B_3^{\phantom\top} & \cdots & 0 \\
\vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & F_{N-2}^{\phantom\top} & B_{N-1}^{\phantom\top}
\end{pmatrix}, \\
\mathcal{S} &= \begin{pmatrix}
S_0^{\phantom\top} \\
& S_1^{\phantom\top} \\
&& S_2^{\phantom\top} \\
&&& S_3^{\phantom\top} \\
&&&& \ddots \\
&&&&& S_{N-1}^{\phantom\top}
\end{pmatrix}.
\end{aligned}
\] The function is called with arguments (iS, S, sync_S, iB, B, iF, F), with indices iS, iB, iF in [0, p) and mutable views S, B, F of the batches of depth v where the diagonal blocks B(iB+l*p) and the subdiagonal blocks F(iB+l*p) of the update matrix and the diagonal elements S(iS+l*p) for l in [0, v) should be stored. Copying non-compact data to these batches can be achieved using the fancyqlone::linalg::pack function. The argument sync_S is a callable that can be called to indicate that the diagonal batch S(iS+l*p) has been fully initialized. It should be accepted by reference (auto &). The rank argument specifies the rank of the update for column with index ctx.index.
